- op: discuss  # 71e9
  at: '2026-09-10T01:28:19Z'  # 71e9
  by: agent  # 71e9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 71e9
  clock: 3  # 71e9
  nonce: '71e9'  # 71e9
  message: "CLOSED 2026-09-09 on behavioural evidence, PR #872 (dev). Measurement:\ndocs/measurements/0027-objc-macro-parse-recovery.md. Lab:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lafom_objc_parse_09092026/.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN FIRST REQUIREMENT, DISCHARGED. Each trigger was established by\nparsing the construct IN ISOLATION, never by reading the source at the first\nERROR node's line. Three families error; the item named one of them, and only\nin a position it did not identify:\n\n    NS_ASSUME_NONNULL_BEGIN WRAPPING a declaration     4 ERROR nodes alone\n    typedef NS_ENUM / NS_OPTIONS / NS_CLOSED_ENUM      3\n    <PREFIX>_API_AVAILABLE(...) and the NS_/API_ family  1 (820 in its file)\n\nREFUTED from the item's own suspect list: `nullable`, generics, block\nproperties, NS_DESIGNATED_INITIALIZER, NS_SWIFT_NAME, FOUNDATION_EXPORT,\n`@property (class, ...)` and a LONE NS_ASSUME_NONNULL_BEGIN all parse with ZERO\nERROR nodes.\n\nTHE GRAMMAR-BUMP BRANCH OF THE ITEM'S DECISION TREE IS CLOSED, NOT SKIPPED.\n3.0.0 / 3.0.1 / 3.0.2 are all that is published and 3.0.2 is installed; upstream's\nlast substantive commit is 2024-12-16 and tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-objc#21\n(\"bug: does not recognize NS_OPTIONS\") has been open since 2025-02-25. So the\npreprocessing branch is the one taken, via INV-bisok's parse_source hook.\n\nMEASURED, four repositories, 387 files:\n\n    ERROR files      74 -> 38   (19.1% -> 9.8%)\n    ERROR nodes    1687 -> 265\n    MISSING nodes   305 -> 98\n    property_decl   436 -> 491\n    class_interface 322 -> 349\n    symbols          AFNetworking +133, CocoaLumberjack +59, fmdb +160\n\nCONSEQUENCE 1 (the filed motivation) CLOSED END TO END. AFNetworking's\nobjc-reached primitives 12 -> 21 and net_recv 0 -> 2, with six NSURLSession rows\nreaching for the first time (dataTaskWithRequest:, dataTaskWithURL:,\ndownloadTaskWithRequest:, uploadTaskWithRequest:fromData:/fromFile:,\nuploadTaskWithStreamedRequest:). That is measurement 0026's pre-registered\nprediction, refuted then, resolved now against the INPUT rather than the fix.\nNOTE FOR THE RECORD: recovering the HEADER did not do it. With the first two\nrules `session` becomes a property_declaration and net_recv is STILL 0, because\nthe calls live in AFURLSessionManager.m. The blocker moved from .h to .m and had\nto be found a second time.\n\nCONSEQUENCE 2 CLOSED. AFURLSessionManager enters _project_classes (False -> True)\nand the `_declared not in project_classes` guard fires: 41 edges re-key\nAFURLSessionManager -> external, 0 sites lost, 0 gained -- the ~40 this item\npredicted. A precision gain that reads as a count drop.\n\nCONSEQUENCE 3 REDUCED, NOT CLOSED, and filed: see the three residual items.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG AND CORRECTED, both recorded in the measurement:\n  1. The first NS_ENUM rule produced a NEW parse failure (`typedef enum S {...};`\n     has no declarator -> MISSING type_identifier). Caught by counting MISSING\n     separately from ERROR.\n  2. The availability rule was DROPPED on a real number that was not measuring it\n     -- Apple's eighteen names spelled exactly recover ZERO files, because\n     AFNetworking writes AF_API_AVAILABLE. The FILE COUNT hid it a second time\n     (39 -> 38 files while ERROR nodes fell 1094 -> 265).\n  3. Byte-length preservation is NOT the whole hook contract: blanking a\n     multi-line API_DEPRECATED destroys a newline and shifts every following\n     span's LINE. The corpus numbers are identical either way, which is why only\n     a newline-count assertion could find it."  # 71e9
